    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where F : Rd → Rn is referred as forward operator, and η represents the measurement noise, which is assumed to follow an n-dimensional Gaussian distribution. In the Bayesian framework, the vectors x, η and y are treated as random variables. Assuming that x and η are independent with π0 as the prior distribution and η ∼ N(0,Σ) as the Gaussian noise. The joint distribution of (x,y) is expressed as"
